The next logical step is to handle the case where an item is too large to fit entirely in the live region. The current design intends to display a truncated tail of such an oversized item in the live area, while the full item is stored in the static scrollback. To make this behavior explicit, each `Item` should be able to indicate whether it is a "tail‑only" placeholder—i.e., only the tail part is being shown because the full content lives elsewhere. This flag will be used by the rendering logic to decide whether to render the full text or just the tail, and also by the cleanup code that drops the placeholder when the next item arrives.

